        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "None of the human coding was included in the LLM prompt. The LLM is thus evaluated against labels it has not seen.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Section 3.2 says the output quality was reviewed after the first run, the prompt was updated, and the validation set analysis was repeated. The manuscript does not say whether the reviewed output was the validation set or whether human labels informed the prompt edits. The reported Tables 3 and 4 therefore reflect a prompt that was tuned after at least one look at the same 34 articles. The first-run validation results are not reported, so sensitivity to the prompt revision cannot be assessed. The prompt change concerned geographic fields and wider infrastructure, not obviously the relevance rule, so the effect on the relevance agreement may be small; this cannot be verified from the text.",
