      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Table 4's note says it uses the majority of three runs. Section 3.2 describes each article as analysed by an individual API call, with temperature at its default. The text reports repeated runs only for the validation set and the full-run description is silent on repetition. If the full run is a single draw, the validated majority-vote result is not the deployed estimand. The one inconsistent article (3%) shows that single-run output can differ from the majority, but the paper does not report single-run agreement. This is a disclosure gap; the implementation of the full run is not established either way.",
